        "prerequisite_note": "Complete the earlier Debian package unit first: installed records, refreshing lists, dependencies and safe removal are reused. This lesson adds repository file lookup; it does not run a command from the files it finds.",
        "concepts": [
          {
            "title": "File names and package names differ",
            "text": "A package bundles files under a package name. A missing /usr/bin/exhibit-audit might come from a differently named package. dpkg-query -S only searches installed records. An unknown owner is useful evidence, not a repair."
          },
          {
            "title": "Search available files",
            "text": "apt-file reads repository Contents metadata, including uninstalled packages. apt-file search exhibit-audit matches a literal part of a file name. apt-file -F search usr/bin/exhibit-audit matches the complete path. Printed paths omit the first slash; usr/bin and usr/libexec are different locations."
          },
          {
            "title": "Inspect, then install",
            "text": "The result format is package-name: path. apt-file list PACKAGE lists that package\u2019s available file paths without installing it. In this sample, apt-get --error-on=any update refreshes both metadata lists. Search does not depend on the package already being installed, and it never changes software."
          }
        ],
        "example_description": "Workshop: the missing /usr/bin/exhibit-audit must be installed while keeping gallery-viewer, gallery-lib and /work/gallery-notes.txt. The old index has lookalikes but lacks the needed executable. Refresh, search and inspect the complete path before installing. This example uses separate workshop packages.",
        "example_actions": [
          {
            "action": {
              "kind": "RefreshIndex"
            },
            "command": "apt-get --error-on=any update",
            "explanation": "Refresh metadata, then type apt-file search exhibit-audit. Compare the printed paths. Narrow with apt-file -F search usr/bin/exhibit-audit and inspect apt-file list gallery-tools; these queries do not install anything."
          },
          {
            "action": {
              "kind": "Install",
              "packages": [
                {
                  "name": "gallery-tools",
                  "version": null
                }
              ]
            },
            "command": "apt-get -y install gallery-tools",
            "explanation": "The complete executable path belongs to gallery-tools. Install it, then use Check work; the library and viewer stay unchanged."
          }
        ],
        "try_change": {
          "description": "After the workshop passes, install gallery-private. It adds a similar-name file under usr/libexec, so the required executable still works but the no-lookalike requirement fails. Compare both complete paths with apt-file search exhibit-audit. Remove gallery-private to repair the task.",
          "actions": [
            {
              "kind": "Install",
              "packages": [
                {
                  "name": "gallery-private",
                  "version": null
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "expected": [
            true,
            true,
            true,
            true,
            true,
            true,
            true,
            true,
            false,
            true
          ]
        },
        "repair": [
          {
            "kind": "Remove",
            "name": "gallery-private"
          }
        ]
      },
      "explanation": "The installed ownership database cannot identify software that has not been installed. The refreshed Contents index maps the exact usr/bin/ledger-check path to records-tools; the documentation and usr/libexec matches are different files. Installing that package satisfies its declared library dependency without adding either lookalike or disturbing the viewer and notes."
    }
